            <ArticleTitle>Clinically useful monoclonal antibodies in treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Monoclonal antibodies have been used in clinical diagnosis for many years but it is only now that these agents are being licensed for clinical treatments. This review will focus on UK licensed monoclonal antibodies highlighting their clinical benefits, limitations, and side effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
